AGENT-README: {{ model.assembly_name }}
A .NET wrapper around the Rust crate {{ model.crate_name }}
================================================================================

If you are an AI coding agent using this library: read this file in full.
It was generated together with the wrapper.


OVERVIEW
========

{{ model.assembly_name }} is a .NET 10 class library around the Rust crate
{{ model.crate_name }}. It holds the crate's native library for these runtime
identifiers: {{ model.runtime_identifiers_text }}.
{{~ if model.is_pass_through ~}}
The crate exports C functions itself; each one is a static method of
{{ model.lib_class_name }}.
{{~ else ~}}
The crate's public API is reached through a generated C facade: Rust objects
are disposable classes, plain Rust structs are readonly record structs, C-like
enums are C# enums, Rust errors are {{ model.exception_class_name }}.
{{~ end ~}}
Generated by CodeBrix.RustTools.CrateBuilder; do not edit the generated files
(regenerating rewrites them). Every generated type is partial.


REFERENCE / INSTALLATION
========================

    <ProjectReference Include="path/to/{{ model.assembly_name }}/{{ model.assembly_name }}.csproj" />
{{~ if model.is_packable ~}}

or, packed with `dotnet pack -c Release -o <feed folder>`, the NuGet package
(that folder added as a package source):

    <PackageReference Include="{{ model.packaging.package_id }}" Version="<version of the .nupkg>" />

Every pack gets a new date-stamped version (1.<years>.<day>.<minute>, UTC);
the .nupkg file name carries it. The package holds the native files under
runtimes/<rid>/native/ as well.
{{~ end ~}}

The native files are copied to runtimes/<rid>/native/ in the output folder of
every project that references this one. Target framework: net10.0.
{{~ if model.links_web_gpu ~}}
The crate links the CodeBrix WebGPU engine: the wrapper references
CodeBrix.WebGpu.Native.MitLicenseForever and calls
CodeBrixWebGpuNative.EnsureLoaded() before it loads the crate's library.
{{~ end ~}}


